id: pm-graph-triplicate
title: Render package visuals with build-time Triplicate tokens
description: "Restyle every diagram format from pinned pm-brand values; preserve export behavior and prove light/dark accessibility with real tracker renders, regression and revert evidence."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T09:27:51.195Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T11:39:42.861Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:28:13.055Z",codex-agent,"Design: form-paper canvas and ruled top sheets; carbon text, Martian Mono ids and dates, explicit status labels and contract chip fills. Canary and rose only convey in_progress and blocked. Brand values are generated at build time from an exact devDependency; published runtime has no brand dependency or CDN fetches. Existing scheduling, graph edges and serialization stay intact."
  "2026-10-17T10:12:53.675Z",codex-agent,"Visual formats are Mermaid flowcharts, DOT and PlantUML; interchange schemas remain unchanged. Each uses ruled sheets, a real mono form strip and explicit filled/outlined status cells. DOT/PlantUML accept literal dark palettes through renderer arguments; Mermaid adapts scoped CSS. Browser review caught ignored directives and variables rejected in Mermaid source style declarations; these now use a leading directive, scoped CSS values and a literal border declaration. Behavioral revert proof restores only each of the three renderers in turn: the unchanged real-tracker regression fails 1/1 each; the restored implementation passes 1/1. The README embeds pm-brand banner commit 5c80a2b707f3a00afe986e81e520843b86f3ee83. Full gates are pending."
  "2026-10-17T10:50:59.381Z",codex-agent,"Render review caught a Mermaid canvas rule rejected because bare declarations preceded it. Removed the invalid declarations and themed nested edge-label backgrounds. Real-tracker focused tests pass 5/5; scoped renderer revert proofs remain 1/1 failures for each of Mermaid, DOT and PlantUML, with 1/1 passes restored. Full computed-color browser checks and release gates are being rerun on the corrected implementation."
  "2026-10-17T11:29:18.305Z",codex-agent,"Both CI-isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass: each 352/352 tests; 99.72% lines, 95.24% branches and 100% functions over all 13 intended runtime sources, zero failed, canceled or skipped tests. The pinned pm runner passes focused tests 5/5; project test execution tracking remains disabled by existing policy, so results are recorded here. Published 72 before/after PNGs on pr-screenshots, with 36 after cases passing widths/themes/scales, no overflow, animations, interactive actions or external requests. Renderer hashes match the published evidence. Independent renderer reverts fail 1/1 each and restored renderers pass 1/1. Strict CI-isolated tracker health passes with existing advisories retained. CI retains Node 22 coverage and runs both full release gates on Node 26 without a redundant third coverage run. No brand token gap found; pm-brand release remains held. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress."
  "2026-10-17T11:35:00.919Z",codex-agent,"CI on Bun 1.4.3 failed before the full release checks: npm-lock migration compared the Git kit download with npm prepared-archive integrity. A fresh-cache minimal reproduction fails with the original entry and passes when only that optional integrity field is removed. The exact approved commit and all registry dependency integrity values stay pinned. Applying this lock-only repair and validating fresh npm and Bun installs; renderer values and published PNGs remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-17T11:39:41.152Z",codex-agent,"Fresh npm ci and clean-cache Bun 1.4.3 install both pass after removing only the optional integrity field from the exact Git dependency. brand:check and a fresh build pass; committed dist and renderer hashes are unchanged. The original lock entry reproduces IntegrityCheckFailed, while the commit-only entry installs successfully. Registry integrity checks remain intact. Full npm/Bun runtime gate evidence is unchanged; CI will rerun both complete release gates on this installation-metadata repair. Kit release remains held."
